From b8db4e0987729e4934a51f55ad38e1b0ddb4ff56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:52:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/31] phy: apple: t6050-usb2: port 1 from the inherited
 state, test switches

Port 1 skips the USB 2.0 flip and starts the SuperSpeed sequence from the
state the kernel inherits, which equals the state the proxy runs started
from; the inherited registers are logged. Step 13 waits up to 1 s for the
SS port's warm reset to complete, so the xHCI reset in step 17 leaves a
clean port as in the proxy runs. The per-step trace records the SS PORTSC.

Boot parameters, all off by default:
- ss_flip: flipped plug orientation (lane 1, swapped crossbar, lane swap)
- ss_susphy_clear: clear GUSB3PIPECTL SUSPHY after the xHCI reset
- ss_replug_s: simulated disconnect through the port's Type-C controller
  after step 16
- ss_u2resets: extra USB 2.0 port resets until the SS port connects
- ss_standalone: the sequence and the USB 2.0 resets without the xHCI
  driver

SuperSpeed on port 1 does not come up reliably yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1fec24ca4e2e840f85fc625b4f8dbe855c76e750)
